 fields in the destination.","docMarkdown":"EnableDecoderDisallowUnknownFields is used to call the DisallowUnknownFields method on the JSON Decoder instance. DisallowUnknownFields causes the Decoder to return an error when the destination is a struct and the input contains object keys which do not match any non-ignored, exported fields in the destination.","declaration":"var EnableDecoderDisallowUnknownFields = false","position":{"file":"binding/json.go","line":25}},{"name":"EnableDecoderUseNumber","doc":"EnableDecoderUseNumber is used to call the UseNumber method on the JSON\nDecoder instance. UseNumber causes the Decoder to unmarshal a number into an\nany as a Number instead of as a float64.","docMarkdown":"EnableDecoderUseNumber is used to call the UseNumber method on the JSON Decoder instance. UseNumber causes the Decoder to unmarshal a number into an any as a Number instead of as a float64.","declaration":"var EnableDecoderUseNumber = false","position":{"file":"binding/json.go","line":19}},{"name":"Validator","doc":"Validator is the default validator which implements the StructValidator\ninterface. It uses https://github.com/go-playground/validator/tree/v10.6.1\nunder the hood.","docMarkdown":"Validator is the default validator which implements the StructValidator interface. It uses [https://github.com/go-playground/validator/tree/v10.6.1](https://github.com/go-playground/validator/tree/v10.6.1) under the hood.","declaration":"var Validator StructValidator = &defaultValidator{}","position":{"file":"binding/binding.go","line":72}}],"funcs":[{"name":"Default","doc":"Default returns the appropriate Binding instance based on the HTTP method\nand the content type.","docMarkdown":"Default returns the appropriate Binding instance based on the HTTP method and the content type.","signature":"func Default(method, contentType string) Binding","position":{"file":"binding/binding.go","line":95},"examples":[]},{"name":"MapFormWithTag","doc":"","signature":"func MapFormWithTag(ptr any, form map[string][]string, tag string) error","position":{"file":"binding/form_mapping.go","line":40},"examples":[]}],"types":[{"name":"BindUnmarshaler","doc":"BindUnmarshaler is the interface used to wrap the UnmarshalParam method.","docMarkdown":"BindUnmarshaler is the interface used to wrap the UnmarshalParam method.","declaration":"type BindUnmarshaler interface {\n\t// UnmarshalParam decodes and assigns a value from a form or query param.\n\tUnmarshalParam(param string) error\n}","kind":"interface","position":{"file":"binding/form_mapping.go","line":183},"fields":[{"name":"UnmarshalParam","doc":"UnmarshalParam decodes and assigns a value from a form or query param.","docMarkdown":"UnmarshalParam decodes and assigns a value from a form or query param.","type":"func(param string) error"}],"methods":[],"examples":[]},{"name":"Binding","doc":"Binding describes the interface which needs to be implemented for binding the\ndata present in the request such as JSON request body, query parameters or\nthe form POST.","docMarkdown":"Binding describes the interface which needs to be implemented for binding the data present in the request such as JSON request body, query parameters or the form POST.","declaration":"type Binding interface {\n\tName() string\n\tBind(*http.Request, any) error\n}","kind":"interface","position":{"file":"binding/binding.go","line":32},"fields":[{"name":"Name","doc":"","type":"func() string"},{"name":"Bind","doc":"","type":"func(*http.Request, any) error"}],"methods":[],"examples":[]},{"name":"BindingBody","doc":"BindingBody adds BindBody method to Binding. BindBody is similar with Bind,\nbut it reads the body from supplied bytes instead of req.Body.","docMarkdown":"BindingBody adds BindBody method to Binding. BindBody is similar with Bind, but it reads the body from supplied bytes instead of req.Body.","declaration":"type BindingBody interface {\n\tBinding\n\tBindBody([]byte, any) error\n}","kind":"interface","position":{"file":"binding/binding.go","line":39},"fields":[{"name":"Binding","doc":"","type":"Binding","embedded":true},{"name":"BindBody","doc":"","type":"func([]byte, any) error"}],"methods":[],"examples":[]},{"name":"BindingUri","doc":"BindingUri adds BindUri method to Binding. BindUri is similar with Bind,\nbut it reads the Params.","docMarkdown":"BindingUri adds BindUri method to Binding. BindUri is similar with Bind, but it reads the Params.","declaration":"type BindingUri interface {\n\tName() string\n\tBindUri(map[string][]string, any) error\n}","kind":"interface","position":{"file":"binding/binding.go","line":46},"fields":[{"name":"Name","doc":"","type":"func() string"},{"name":"BindUri","doc":"","type":"func(map[string][]string, any) error"}],"methods":[],"examples":[]},{"name":"SliceValidationError","doc":"","declaration":"type SliceValidationError []error","kind":"defined","position":{"file":"binding/default_validator.go","line":21},"fields":[],"methods":[{"name":"Error","doc":"Error concatenates all error elements in SliceValidationError into a single string separated by \\n.","docMarkdown":"Error concatenates all error elements in SliceValidationError into a single string separated by \\\\n.","signature":"func (err SliceValidationError) Error() string","position":{"file":"binding/default_validator.go","line":24},"examples":[]}],"examples":[]},{"name":"StructValidator","doc":"StructValidator is the minimal interface which needs to be implemented in\norder for it to be used as the validator engine for ensuring the correctness\nof the request. Gin provides a default implementation for this using\nhttps://github.com/go-playground/validator/tree/v10.6.1.","docMarkdown":"StructValidator is the minimal interface which needs to be implemented in order for it to be used as the validator engine for ensuring the correctness of the request. Gin provides a default implementation for this using [https://github.com/go-playground/validator/tree/v10.6.1](https://github.com/go-playground/validator/tree/v10.6.1).","declaration":"type StructValidator interface {\n\t// ValidateStruct can receive any kind of type and it should never panic, even if the configuration is not right.\n\t// If the received type is a slice|array, the validation should be performed travel on every element.\n\t// If the received type is not a struct or slice|array, any validation should be skipped and nil must be returned.\n\t// If the received type is a struct or pointer to a struct, the validation should be performed.\n\t// If the struct is not valid or the validation itself fails, a descriptive error should be returned.\n\t// Otherwise nil must be returned.\n\tValidateStruct(any) error\n\n\t// Engine returns the underlying validator engine which powers the\n\t// StructValidator implementation.\n\tEngine() any\n}","kind":"interface","position":{"file":"binding/binding.go","line":55},"fields":[{"name":"ValidateStruct","doc":"ValidateStruct can receive any kind of type and it should never panic, even if the configuration is not right.\nIf the received type is a slice|array, the validation should be performed travel on every element.\nIf the received type is not a struct or slice|array, any validation should be skipped and nil must be returned.\nIf the received type is a struct or pointer to a struct, the validation should be performed.\nIf the struct is not valid or the validation itself fails, a descriptive error should be returned.\nOtherwise nil must be returned.","docMarkdown":"ValidateStruct can receive any kind of type and it should never panic, even if the configuration is not right. If the received type is a slice|array, the validation should be performed travel on every element. If the received type is not a struct or slice|array, any validation should be skipped and nil must be returned. If the received type is a struct or pointer to a struct, the validation should be performed. If the struct is not valid or the validation itself fails, a descriptive error should be returned. Otherwise nil must be returned.","type":"func(any) error"},{"name":"Engine","doc":"Engine returns the underlying validator engine which powers the\nStructValidator implementation.","docMarkdown":"Engine returns the underlying validator engine which powers the StructValidator implementation.","type":"func() any"}],"methods":[],"examples":[]}],"examples":[]},{"importPath":"github.com/gin-gonic/gin/codec/json","name":"json","synopsis":"","doc":"","dir":"codec/json","files":["codec/json/api.go","codec/json/json.go"],"consts":[{"name":"Package","doc":"Package indicates what library is being used for JSON encoding.","docMarkdown":"Package indicates what library is being used for JSON encoding.","declaration":"const Package = \"encoding/json\"","position":{"file":"codec/json/json.go","line":15}}],"vars":[{"name":"API","doc":"API the json codec in use.","docMarkdown":"API the json codec in use.","declaration":"var API Core","position":{"file":"codec/json/api.go","line":10}}],"funcs":[],"types":[{"name":"Core","doc":"Core the api for json codec.","docMarkdown":"Core the api for json codec.","declaration":"type Core interface {\n\tMarshal(v any) ([]byte, error)\n\tUnmarshal(data []byte, v any) error\n\tMarshalIndent(v any, prefix, indent string) ([]byte, error)\n\tNewEncoder(writer io.Writer) Encoder\n\tNewDecoder(reader io.Reader) Decoder\n}","kind":"interface","position":{"file":"codec/json/api.go","line":13},"fields":[{"name":"Marshal","doc":"","type":"func(v any) ([]byte, error)"},{"name":"Unmarshal","doc":"","type":"func(data []byte, v any) error"},{"name":"MarshalIndent","doc":"","type":"func(v any, prefix, indent string) ([]byte, error)"},{"name":"NewEncoder","doc":"","type":"func(writer io.Writer) Encoder"},{"name":"NewDecoder","doc":"","type":"func(reader io.Reader) Decoder"}],"methods":[],"examples":[]},{"name":"Decoder","doc":"Decoder an interface reads and decodes JSON values from an input stream.","docMarkdown":"Decoder an interface reads and decodes JSON values from an input stream.","declaration":"type Decoder interface {\n\t// UseNumber causes the Decoder to unmarshal a number into an any as a\n\t// Number instead of as a float64.\n\tUseNumber()\n\n\t// DisallowUnknownFields causes the Decoder to return an error when the destination\n\t// is a struct and the input contains object keys which do not match any\n\t// non-ignored, exported fields in the destination.\n\tDisallowUnknownFields()\n\n\t// Decode reads the next JSON-encoded value from its\n\t// input and stores it in the value pointed to by v.\n\t//\n\t// See the documentation for Unmarshal for details about\n\t// the conversion of JSON into a Go value.\n\tDecode(v any) error\n}","kind":"interface","position":{"file":"codec/json/api.go","line":41},"fields":[{"name":"UseNumber","doc":"UseNumber causes the Decoder to unmarshal a number into an any as a\nNumber instead of as a float64.","docMarkdown":"UseNumber causes the Decoder to unmarshal a number into an any as a Number instead of as a float64.","type":"func()"},{"name":"DisallowUnknownFields","doc":"DisallowUnknownFields causes the Decoder to return an error when the destination\nis a struct and the input contains object keys which do not match any\nnon-ignored, exported fields in the destination.","docMarkdown":"DisallowUnknownFields causes the Decoder to return an error when the destination is a struct and the input contains object keys which do not match any non-ignored, exported fields in the destination.","type":"func()"},{"name":"Decode","doc":"Decode reads the next JSON-encoded value from its\ninput and stores it in the value pointed to by v.\n\nSee the documentation for Unmarshal for details about\nthe conversion of JSON into a Go value.","docMarkdown":"Decode reads the next JSON-encoded value from its input and stores it in the value pointed to by v.\n\nSee the documentation for Unmarshal for details about the conversion of JSON into a Go value.","type":"func(v any) error"}],"methods":[],"examples":[]},{"name":"Encoder","doc":"Encoder an interface writes JSON values to an output stream.","docMarkdown":"Encoder an interface writes JSON values to an output stream.","declaration":"type Encoder interface {\n\t// SetEscapeHTML specifies whether problematic HTML characters\n\t// should be escaped inside JSON quoted strings.\n\t// The default behavior is to escape &, <, and > to \\u0026, \\u003c, and \\u003e\n\t// to avoid certain safety problems that can arise when embedding JSON in HTML.\n\t//\n\t// In non-HTML settings where the escaping interferes with the readability\n\t// of the output, SetEscapeHTML(false) disables this behavior.\n\tSetEscapeHTML(on bool)\n\n\t// Encode writes the JSON encoding of v to the stream,\n\t// followed by a newline character.\n\t//\n\t// See the documentation for Marshal for details about the\n\t// conversion of Go values to JSON.\n\tEncode(v any) error\n}","kind":"interface","position":{"file":"codec/json/api.go","line":22},"fields":[{"name":"SetEscapeHTML","doc":"SetEscapeHTML specifies whether problematic HTML characters\nshould be escaped inside JSON quoted strings.\nThe default behavior is to escape &, <, and > to \\u0026, \\u003c, and \\u003e\nto avoid certain safety problems that can arise when embedding JSON in HTML.\n\nIn non-HTML settings where the escaping interferes with the readability\nof the output, SetEscapeHTML(false) disables this behavior.","docMarkdown":"SetEscapeHTML specifies whether problematic HTML characters should be escaped inside JSON quoted strings. The default behavior is to escape &, \\<, and > to \\\\u0026, \\\\u003c, and \\\\u003e to avoid certain safety problems that can arise when embedding JSON in HTML.\n\nIn non-HTML settings where the escaping interferes with the readability of the output, SetEscapeHTML(false) disables this behavior.","type":"func(on bool)"},{"name":"Encode","doc":"Encode writes the JSON encoding of v to the stream,\nfollowed by a newline character.\n\nSee the documentation for Marshal for details about the\nconversion of Go values to JSON.","docMarkdown":"Encode writes the JSON encoding of v to the stream, followed by a newline character.\n\nSee the documentation for Marshal for details about the conversion of Go values to JSON.","type":"func(v any) error"}],"methods":[],"examples":[]}],"examples":[]},{"importPath":"github.com/gin-gonic/gin/ginS","name":"ginS","synopsis":"","doc":"","dir":"ginS","files":["ginS/gins.go"],"consts":[],"vars":[],"funcs":[{"name":"Any","doc":"Any is a wrapper for Engine.Any.","docMarkdown":"Any is a wrapper for Engine.Any.","signature":"func Any(relativePath string, handlers ...gin.HandlerFunc) gin.IRoutes","position":{"file":"ginS/gins.go","line":101},"examples":[]},{"name":"DELETE","doc":"DELETE is a shortcut for router.Handle(\"DELETE\", path, handle)","docMarkdown":"DELETE is a shortcut for router.Handle(\"DELETE\", path, handle)","signature":"func DELETE(relativePath string, handlers ...gin.HandlerFunc) gin.IRoutes","position":{"file":"ginS/gins.go","line":76},"examples":[]},{"name":"GET","doc":"GET is a shortcut for router.Handle(\"GET\", path, handle)","docMarkdown":"GET is a shortcut for router.Handle(\"GET\", path, handle)","signature":"func GET(relativePath string, handlers ...gin.HandlerFunc) gin.IRoutes","position":{"file":"ginS/gins.go","line":66},"examples":[]},{"name":"Group","doc":"Group creates a new router group. You should add all the routes that have common middlewares or the same path prefix.\nFor example, all the routes that use a common middleware for authorization could be grouped.","docMarkdown":"Group creates a new router group. You should add all the routes that have common middlewares or the same path prefix. For example, all the routes that use a common middleware for authorization could be grouped.","signature":"func Group(relativePath string, handlers ...gin.HandlerFunc) *gin.RouterGroup","position":{"file":"ginS/gins.go","line":51},"examples":[]},{"name":"HEAD","doc":"HEAD is a shortcut for router.Handle(\"HEAD\", path, handle)","docMarkdown":"HEAD is a shortcut for router.Handle(\"HEAD\", path, handle)","signature":"func HEAD(relativePath string, handlers ...gin.HandlerFunc) gin.IRoutes","position":{"file":"ginS/gins.go","line":96},"examples":[]},{"name":"Handle","doc":"Handle is a wrapper for Engine.Handle.","docMarkdown":"Handle is a wrapper for Engine.Handle.","signature":"func Handle(httpMethod, relativePath string, handlers ...gin.HandlerFunc) gin.IRoutes","position":{"file":"ginS/gins.go","line":56},"examples":[]},{"name":"LoadHTMLFS","doc":"LoadHTMLFS is a wrapper for Engine.LoadHTMLFS.","docMarkdown":"LoadHTMLFS is a wrapper for Engine.LoadHTMLFS.","signature":"func LoadHTMLFS(fs http.FileSystem, patterns ...string)","position":{"file":"ginS/gins.go","line":30},"examples":[]},{"name":"LoadHTMLFiles","doc":"LoadHTMLFiles is a wrapper for Engine.LoadHTMLFiles.","docMarkdown":"LoadHTMLFiles is a wrapper for Engine.LoadHTMLFiles.","signature":"func LoadHTMLFiles(files ...string)","position":{"file":"ginS/gins.go","line":25},"examples":[]},{"name":"LoadHTMLGlob","doc":"LoadHTMLGlob is a wrapper for Engine.LoadHTMLGlob.","docMarkdown":"LoadHTMLGlob is a wrapper for Engine.LoadHTMLGlob.","signature":"func LoadHTMLGlob(pattern string)","position":{"file":"ginS/gins.go","line":20},"examples":[]},{"name":"NoMethod","doc":"NoMethod is a wrapper for Engine.NoMethod.","docMarkdown":"NoMethod is a wrapper for Engine.NoMethod.","signature":"func NoMethod(handlers ...gin.HandlerFunc)","position":{"file":"ginS/gins.go","line":45},"examples":[]},{"name":"NoRoute","doc":"NoRoute adds handlers for NoRoute. It returns a 404 code by default.","docMarkdown":"NoRoute adds handlers for NoRoute. It returns a 404 code by default.","signature":"func NoRoute(handlers ...gin.HandlerFunc)","position":{"file":"ginS/gins.go","line":40},"examples":[]},{"name":"OPTIONS","doc":"OPTIONS is a shortcut for router.Handle(\"OPTIONS\", path, handle)","docMarkdown":"OPTIONS is a shortcut for router.Handle(\"OPTIONS\", path, handle)","signature":"func OPTIONS(relativePath string, handlers ...gin.HandlerFunc) gin.IRoutes","position":{"file":"ginS/gins.go","line":91},"examples":[]},{"name":"PATCH","doc":"PATCH is a shortcut for router.Handle(\"PATCH\", path, handle)","docMarkdown":"PATCH is a shortcut for router.Handle(\"PATCH\", path, handle)","signature":"func PATCH(relativePath string, handlers ...gin.HandlerFunc) gin.IRoutes","position":{"file":"ginS/gins.go","line":81},"examples":[]},{"name":"POST","doc":"POST is a shortcut for router.Handle(\"POST\", path, handle)","docMarkdown":"POST is a shortcut for router.Handle(\"POST\", path, handle)","signature":"func POST(relativePath string, handlers ...gin.HandlerFunc) gin.IRoutes","position":{"file":"ginS/gins.go","line":61},"examples":[]},{"name":"PUT","doc":"PUT is a shortcut for router.Handle(\"PUT\", path, handle)","docMarkdown":"PUT is a shortcut for router.Handle(\"PUT\", path, handle)","signature":"func PUT(relativePath string, handlers ...gin.HandlerFunc) gin.IRoutes","position":{"file":"ginS/gins.go","line":86},"examples":[]},{"name":"QUERY","doc":"QUERY is a shortcut for router.Handle(\"QUERY\", path, handle)","docMarkdown":"QUERY is a shortcut for router.Handle(\"QUERY\", path, handle)","signature":"func QUERY(relativePath string, handlers ...gin.HandlerFunc) gin.IRoutes","position":{"file":"ginS/gins.go","line":71},"examples":[]},{"name":"Routes","doc":"Routes returns a slice of registered routes.","docMarkdown":"Routes returns a slice of registered routes.","signature":"func Routes() gin.RoutesInfo","position":{"file":"ginS/gins.go","line":134},"examples":[]},{"name":"Run","doc":"Run attaches to a http.Server and starts listening and serving HTTP requests.\nIt is a shortcut for http.ListenAndServe(addr, router)\nNote: this method will block the calling goroutine indefinitely unless an error happens.","docMarkdown":"Run attaches to a http.Server and starts listening and serving HTTP requests. It is a shortcut for http.ListenAndServe(addr, router) Note: this method will block the calling goroutine indefinitely unless an error happens.","signature":"func Run(addr ...string) (err error)","position":{"file":"ginS/gins.go","line":141},"examples":[]},{"name":"RunFd","doc":"RunFd attaches the router to a http.Server and starts listening and serving HTTP requests\nthrough the specified file descriptor.\nNote: the method will block the calling goroutine indefinitely unless an error happens.","docMarkdown":"RunFd attaches the router to a http.Server and starts listening and serving HTTP requests through the specified file descriptor. Note: the method will block the calling goroutine indefinitely unless an error happens.","signature":"func RunFd(fd int) (err error)","position":{"file":"ginS/gins.go","line":162},"examples":[]},{"name":"RunTLS","doc":"RunTLS attaches to a http.Server and starts listening and serving HTTPS requests.\nIt is a shortcut for http.ListenAndServeTLS(addr, certFile, keyFile, router)\nNote: this method will block the calling goroutine indefinitely unless an error happens.","docMarkdown":"RunTLS attaches to a http.Server and starts listening and serving HTTPS requests. It is a shortcut for http.ListenAndServeTLS(addr, certFile, keyFile, router) Note: this method will block the calling goroutine indefinitely unless an error happens.","signature":"func RunTLS(addr, certFile, keyFile string) (err error)","position":{"file":"ginS/gins.go","line":148},"examples":[]},{"name":"RunUnix","doc":"RunUnix attaches to a http.Server and starts listening and serving HTTP requests\nthrough the specified unix socket (i.e. a file)\nNote: this method will block the calling goroutine indefinitely unless an error happens.","docMarkdown":"RunUnix attaches to a http.Server and starts listening and serving HTTP requests through the specified unix socket (i.e. a file) Note: this method will block the calling goroutine indefinitely unless an error happens.","signature":"func RunUnix(file string) (err error)","position":{"file":"ginS/gins.go","line":155},"examples":[]},{"name":"SetHTMLTemplate","doc":"SetHTMLTemplate is a wrapper for Engine.SetHTMLTemplate.","docMarkdown":"SetHTMLTemplate is a wrapper for Engine.SetHTMLTemplate.","signature":"func SetHTMLTemplate(templ *template.Template)","position":{"file":"ginS/gins.go","line":35},"examples":[]},{"name":"Static","doc":"Static serves files from the given file system root.\nInternally a http.FileServer is used, therefore http.NotFound is used instead\nof the Router's NotFound handler.\nTo use the operating system's file system implementation,\nuse :\n\n\trouter.Static(\"/static\", \"/var/www\")","docMarkdown":"Static serves files from the given file system root. Internally a http.FileServer is used, therefore http.NotFound is used instead of the Router's NotFound handler. To use the operating system's file system implementation, use :\n\n\trouter.Static(\"/static\", \"/var/www\")","signature":"func Static(relativePath, root string) gin.IRoutes","position":{"file":"ginS/gins.go","line":117},"examples":[]},{"name":"StaticFS","doc":"StaticFS is a wrapper for Engine.StaticFS.","docMarkdown":"StaticFS is a wrapper for Engine.StaticFS.","signature":"func StaticFS(relativePath string, fs http.FileSystem) gin.IRoutes","position":{"file":"ginS/gins.go","line":122},"examples":[]},{"name":"StaticFile","doc":"StaticFile is a wrapper for Engine.StaticFile.","docMarkdown":"StaticFile is a wrapper for Engine.StaticFile.","signature":"func StaticFile(relativePath, filepath string) gin.IRoutes","position":{"file":"ginS/gins.go","line":106},"examples":[]},{"name":"Use","doc":"Use attaches a global middleware to the router. i.e. the middlewares attached through Use() will be\nincluded in the handlers chain for every single request. Even 404, 405, static files...\nFor example, this is the right place for a logger or error management middleware.","docMarkdown":"Use attaches a global middleware to the router. i.e. the middlewares attached through Use() will be included in the handlers chain for every single request. Even 404, 405, static files... For example, this is the right place for a logger or error management middleware.","signature":"func Use(middlewares ...gin.HandlerFunc) gin.IRoutes","position":{"file":"ginS/gins.go","line":129},"examples":[]}],"types":[],"examples":[]},{"importPath":"github.com/gin-gonic/gin/render","name":"render","synopsis":"","doc":"","dir":"render","files":["render/bson.go","render/data.go","render/html.go","render/json.go","render/msgpack.go","render/pdf.go","render/protobuf.go","render/reader.go","render/redirect.go","render/render.go","render/text.go","render/toml.go","render/xml.go","render/yaml.go"],"consts":[],"vars":[],"funcs":[{"name":"WriteJSON","doc":"WriteJSON marshals the given interface object and writes it with custom ContentType.","docMarkdown":"WriteJSON marshals the given interface object and writes it with custom ContentType.","signature":"func WriteJSON(w http.ResponseWriter, obj any) error","position":{"file":"render/json.go","line":67},"examples":[]},{"name":"WriteMsgPack","doc":"WriteMsgPack writes MsgPack ContentType and encodes the given interface object.","docMarkdown":"WriteMsgPack writes MsgPack ContentType and encodes the given interface object.","signature":"func WriteMsgPack(w http.ResponseWriter, obj any) error","position":{"file":"render/msgpack.go","line":39},"examples":[]},{"name":"WriteString","doc":"WriteString writes data according to its format and write custom ContentType.","docMarkdown":"WriteString writes data according to its format and write custom ContentType.","signature":"func WriteString(w http.ResponseWriter, format string, data []any) (err error)","position":{"file":"render/text.go","line":33},"examples":[]}],"types":[{"name":"AsciiJSON","doc":"AsciiJSON contains the given interface object.","docMarkdown":"AsciiJSON contains the given interface object.","declaration":